  "case": "oauth-before-sign-in",
  "description": "With OAuth on and lazy sign-in (the default), a host that has not signed in can initialize, list every tool and run the free ones; a paid call, alone or in a batch, gets the 401 challenge carrying its JSON-RPC id. A bearer that is not an agent's is the merchant's unless it calls a paid tool. A body that is not JSON goes to the MCP server's parse error, and a GET (no tool call) to the MCP server. An agent token that does not verify gets the challenge too, saying the sign-in expired or was not accepted, with the request's id (null when there is none). A token a host got by OAuth (aud = the resource, cid) is served.",
